The values is a list of 5, 0, 3, 8, and 6.
The size is the number of items in values.
The last is the last position of values.
The ceilings is a list of size zeros.
Set item 0 of ceilings to item 0 of values.
For every spot from 1 to last.
The prior is item (spot minus 1) of ceilings.
If prior is more than item spot of values, set item spot of ceilings to prior, otherwise set item spot of ceilings to item spot of values.

The floors is a list of size zeros.
Set item last of floors to item last of values.
For every step from 1 to last.
The spot is last minus step.
The after is item (spot plus 1) of floors.
If after is less than item spot of values, set item spot of floors to after, otherwise set item spot of floors to item spot of values.

The boundary is 0.
For every spot from 0 to last minus 1.
The upper is item spot of ceilings.
The lower is item (spot plus 1) of floors.
If upper is at most lower, set boundary to spot plus 1, then stop.

Report boundary.
